# 2026-07-30 implementation notes
- New runtime/durable.c: jinn_atomic_rewrite (write temp in same dir →
  fsync → rename → fsync dir; any failure leaves the original untouched),
  jinn_atomic_rewrite_reopen (for callers holding a long-lived FILE* —
  the old handle points at the replaced inode after rename), checked
  fsync helpers, and the D6 single-writer advisory lock (flock on
  <path>.lock — a stable lock file, never renamed, so the lock cannot be
  lost to a rewrite of the data file).
- Converted: kv.c (now path-based — also fixes deleted-key resurrection
  from stale tails, since a temp file can never carry old trailing
  entries), migrate.c's three close/"w+b"-truncate sites (add_field,
  drop_field, compact), version.c's compact (signature gained the path —
  the function had zero callers), bloom.c's close-persist.
- kv single-writer: jinn_kv_open takes the lock; contention prints the
  D6 diagnostic and returns NULL (all kv API is NULL-tolerant, so ops
  degrade to no-ops after the loud message).
- tests/durable_crash.c + durable_crash.rs: die-mid-fill at every prefix
  (old image always intact), SIGKILL-during-kv-churn ×25 (image always
  complete and self-consistent), and lock refusal/re-admission.
- Store `.store` writes themselves (insert/update/delete paths in
  codegen) still rewrite in place — their crash story is the WAL's
  (8-22/8-23), not per-write rename; the migration/compact paths those
  tasks lean on are now atomic.
